A phone battery question at 23:23. Short answer. 10% overnight is normal — standby drain, background sync, poor signal. Only a concern if it's much worse. Keep it brief since they're going to bed.

2027-01-05T04:23:58  thought   (empty)

2027-01-05T04:23:58  message   To the owner:
Yes, normal. Ten percent over a night is about what standby costs — background sync, wifi, a few push notifications, and the phone waking itself to do housekeeping. Plenty of phones do 5 to 15 percent and it's nothing to worry about.

When it's not normal: 25 percent or more, or the phone noticeably warm when you pick it up, or the drain started suddenly after an update or a new app. That's usually one app stuck awake, and the battery settings screen will name it under usage by app — look at what ran while the screen was off.

Two things that actually help if it bugs you: a weaker signal drains more (the radio hunting for a tower all night), and leaving it off the charger at 100 percent isn't better for it than charging overnight.

Now go to bed — that's twice tonight.

