2027-01-05T05:03:32  message   To the owner:
Twenty minutes at midnight: don't clean, reset. Three things, in this order.

1. The sink (5 min). Dishes out, counters wiped, nothing left in it. A kitchen with an empty sink reads as a clean kitchen even if nothing else is done. A sink with three plates in it reads as a mess no matter how tidy the rest is.

2. The surface you see first (5 min). The table, the counter by the door, the chair things get dumped on — whichever one your eye lands on walking in. Clear it completely, put the pile in a basket or a cupboard, don't sort it. Sorting is what eats twenty minutes.

3. Trash and floor (10 min). One bag round the house for cups, wrappers, post. Then shoes and bags out of the walkway. That's it — no mopping, no folding.

The rule: put things away, don't clean things. Twenty minutes of cleaning looks like nothing happened. Twenty minutes of putting away looks like someone came in.

And whatever's left in your hand when the twenty minutes are up, put it in a cupboard, not back on the table. It's midnight — future you in the morning will care a lot more about a clear counter than a correctly filed pile.

