Short version, since I wrote it up earlier today: red lentils, one pot, forty minutes.

Soften an onion and two carrots in oil for 8 minutes, add three garlic cloves, a tablespoon of tomato paste and a teaspoon each of cumin and paprika, fry a minute until it smells nutty. Add 250g rinsed red lentils and a litre and a quarter of stock. Simmer 20-25 minutes until the lentils collapse. Salt, pepper, and the juice of half a lemon off the heat — that's the step that makes it taste like something.

