2027-01-09T23:26:23  message   To the owner:
About 42 percent. Just under 1 in 2.4.

Do it backwards: the chance of no six on one die is 5/6, so no six on three is (5/6)³ = 125/216 ≈ 58 percent. At least one six is 1 − 0.58 = 0.42.

The mistake to avoid is adding 1/6 three times to get 1/2 — that double-counts rolls with two or three sixes. And if it helps: it takes four dice to pass even odds, at 51.8 percent.

