2027-01-09T23:34:04  message   To the owner:
Rate is what you pay on the money; APR is that plus the fees, all expressed as one yearly percentage. So 6.5% rate with 4,000 in fees could be 6.7% APR.

Compare APRs between lenders — it's the only number that shows which deal is actually cheaper. Only caveat: APR assumes you keep the loan full-term, so if you'll remortgage in five years, a low-fee, slightly higher-rate deal often wins.

