2027-01-09T23:40:04  thought   (empty)

2027-01-09T23:40:04  message   To the owner:
Act fast, and the two rules are: blot, don't rub; cold, never hot.

Press the wine out with a paper towel, then run cold water through the back of the stain so it pushes the wine back out the way it went in. Cover it in salt while it's still wet, leave ten minutes, brush off — the salt pulls the colour out. Then a cool wash with normal detergent, and check it before it goes anywhere near a dryer, because heat sets whatever's left.

If it's still faint after washing: white vinegar on the spot for ten minutes, wash again. Oxygen bleach (colour-safe, not chlorine) is the next step up if it's stubborn.

