2027-01-10T01:08:25  message   To the owner:
Short version: most likely the chain, and it's usually wear rather than breakage.

A worn chain skips forward a link under hard pedalling, in every gear, with a clunk you feel through the pedals. That's the common case.

If it slips in one particular gear when you push hard, it's the cassette — worn teeth, hooked into shark fins, won't hold.

If it jumps between gears on its own, that's adjustment, and it's free.

The check: measure twelve links pin to pin. New is exactly 12 inches; 12 and 1/16 is worn; 12 and 1/8 means chain and cassette both. Don't fit a new chain to a worn cassette — it'll skip worse than before.

You didn't say which kind of slipping it is. One gear or all of them?

