KEE-nwah. Stress on the first syllable.

The spelling is a botanist's doing: it's kinwa in Quechua, which Spanish took as quinua and pronounces exactly as it looks. Latinising it to quinoa made it look classical and left English speakers guessing kwi-NOH-uh. The pronunciation never changed — only the spelling did.

