Three new ones, since you've had yesterday's. Answers at the bottom — don't peek.

1. The warm-up. What has a neck but no head, and two arms but no hands?

2. The good one. A woman shoots her husband, then holds him underwater for five minutes, then hangs him. Ten minutes later they sit down to dinner together. How?

3. The cruel one. A man lives on the twelfth floor. Every day he takes the lift down to the ground and goes to work. Every evening he takes the lift to the eighth floor and walks up the rest — unless it's raining, when he goes straight to the twelfth. Why?

Answers: a shirt; she's a photographer; he's short and can only reach the eighth-floor button, except when he has an umbrella.

Want harder? I've got ones that need paper.

