Two things worth flagging, both useful rather than nagging.

First: this is your second Lisbon neighbourhood. Baixa was the first, on Monday, at 140. Now Alfama at 120. Those are quite different places — Baixa is flat, grid-planned, built after the earthquake; Alfama is the old hill below the castle, medieval street plan, trams, steep stairs. If you're actually going to Lisbon, the choice matters: Baixa is easier on the legs and closer to the river; Alfama is prettier and you'll walk uphill a lot. Say which and I'll settle on it.

